          "explanation": "Article I, Section 7 requires a two-thirds vote in BOTH chambers — not one, both — to override a presidential veto. That is a very high bar. In a 435-member House, that's 290 yes votes; in a 100-member Senate, that's 67. Most vetoes stand because the override threshold is so steep. Simple majority is what gets a bill passed in the first place; three-fifths (60) is the Senate's filibuster cloture threshold (a different procedure).",
