          "explanation": "The founders deliberately split the war power. Article I, Section 8, Clause 11 gives Congress the power 'To declare War.' Article II, Section 2 makes the President 'Commander in Chief of the Army and Navy.' The intent: Congress decides whether to go to war; the President directs the war once underway. The War Powers Resolution (1973) is a STATUTORY response to executive overreach during Vietnam, not the source of the underlying powers. The other answers misstate the structure.",
