          "explanation": "Jury duty, when summoned, is a LEGAL DUTY required by the Constitution (Article III, 6th and 7th Amendments) and federal/state law. Failure to appear can result in contempt, fines, or arrest. Voting is a constitutional RIGHT in most U.S. states, not a duty — only Australia and a few others have compulsory voting. Subscribing to newspapers and volunteering are civic responsibilities — important, but not legal requirements. Other legal duties: obey the law, pay taxes, register for Selective Service (males 18-25), appear when subpoenaed, respond to the Census.",
