          "explanation": "The Declaration of Independence (July 4, 1776), drafted primarily by Thomas Jefferson, articulated the American founding philosophy: that all men are created equal, endowed with unalienable rights (life, liberty, pursuit of happiness), and that governments derive their 'just powers from the consent of the governed.' The Constitution (ratified 1788) is the structural framework — but the Declaration is the philosophical foundation. The Federalist Papers (1787-88) argued for ratification of the Constitution. The Bill of Rights (1791) added the first ten amendments protecting individual liberties.",
